{
  "version": 1,
  "_about": [
    "OCARINA — an adventure-score pack in the spirit of late-90s Nintendo",
    "soundtracks: ocarina and harp over modal strings, a different piece for",
    "every kind of place you walk into.",
    "",
    "ORIGINAL MUSIC. Every melody here was written for this pack. None of it is",
    "transcribed from Ocarina of Time — those pieces are Koji Kondo's and remain",
    "Nintendo's copyright, and packs are made to be shared. What is borrowed is",
    "the idiom, which is not anyone's property: modal harmony, ocarina timbre,",
    "rolled harp, question-and-answer phrasing, and the habit of giving each",
    "region its own theme.",
    "",
    "It would not work as a transcription anyway. The engine picks the key and",
    "mode from your surroundings and transposes everything to fit, so a fixed",
    "tune would be pulled out of shape the moment you walked down the street.",
    "Degrees are relative, so these phrases stay musical wherever they land.",
    "",
    "WHERE EACH PIECE APPEARS, verified against live data for Belmont:",
    "  Eternal Joy Church      -> temple pinned, Sanctum 1.00",
    "  Belmont Park            -> Woodland 1.00",
    "  Disc Golf Course        -> Trial grounds 1.00",
    "  White Sail Inn          -> Tavern 1.00",
    "  Dot's Market / Sweet Retreat -> market pinned, Market square 1.00",
    "  Immaculate Conception School -> Schoolyard 1.00",
    "  Great Miami riverfront  -> Waterside 1.00",
    "",
    "The 30-minute loop north (church, park, disc golf, back past the bar) hits",
    "four of those. To hear the market theme, walk SOUTH to Dot's Market or WEST",
    "to the Sweet Retreat strip — or just jump to the saved places in Explore.",
    "",
    "HOW IT IS PUT TOGETHER",
    "  hyrule-field   the default: pastoral overworld, ocarina and harp",
    "  market-town    pinned in busy shopping and eating streets",
    "  temple         pinned near churches and other sacred ground",
    "  7 cues         layer extra parts, or hand over to one of those themes",
    "",
    "TUNING. Cue thresholds are category SHARES, measured in a real suburb:",
    "  sacred 0.49 by a church, 0.13 elsewhere",
    "  nature 0.39 in a park, 0.00-0.15 elsewhere",
    "  food   0.47 on a restaurant strip, 0.00 in housing",
    "  sport  0.33 at playing fields, nightlife 0.31 outside a bar",
    "Shares are damped where little is mapped, so a dominant category lands",
    "around 0.2-0.4 rather than 1.0. If a cue never fires where you",
    "live, lower its 'min' rather than assuming it is broken."
  ],
